note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note seed/ng/bench/ngbench-sha.om: the last unit of ngbench (D1b). Build, in this order:
note   cat seed/ng/ngbench.om seed/ng/sha256.om seed/ng/bench/ngbench-sha.om | seed/out/omc > ngbench
note ngbench.om comes first because its om2 line must be the unit's first line; this part comes after
note seed/ng/sha256.om because it names sha256.om's globals (sh_dat, sh_dig), and a global must be
note declared before use (functions may be called before their definition). Owner: ng-bench lane.
note hashpb: SHA-256 (sha256.om sh_all over sh_dat) of the file named by gpb into gdg and ghx; returns
note its size; 2^63 only when it is absent (open fails with ENOENT, errno 2); 2^63 + 1 when it is
note present but cannot be used: open fails with any other errno (EACCES, ENOTDIR, ELOOP, ...), a read
note fails (a directory: EISDIR), or it holds len sh_dat (16 MiB) bytes or more. Callers that only need
note "no hash" test ge 2^63; callers that treat "absent" as allowed must refuse 2^63 + 1.
fn hashpb to ulong
fd = fopen gpb 0 get gpbn 0 0 0
if lt fd 0
if eq fd -2
ret 9223372036854775808
end
ret 9223372036854775809
end
n = ulong 0
bad = false
going = true
while going bound 16777217
r = read int fd sh_dat n sub len sh_dat n
if lt r 0
bad = true
going = false
else
if eq r 0
going = false
else
n = add n ulong r
if eq n len sh_dat
bad = true
going = false
end
end
end
end
x = fclose int fd
if bad
ret 9223372036854775809
end
sh_all n
for i ulong 32
put gdg i get sh_dig i
end
tohex
ret n
end
